# Delegate to dsh

**Experimental developer preview. Files and shell use the OS sandbox; network is not sandboxed.**
Use only when the user explicitly requests delegation.

**If the user invoked this skill explicitly ({{command "delegate-dsh"}}), always delegate —
whatever the task size. The user chose the harness.**

Launch command (step 2 below):

{{if eq .Host "claude"}}    pactify sub run dsh --write --worktree --wait 0s --json <<'BRIEF'
    ...complete brief from step 1...
    BRIEF
{{else}}    pactify sub run dsh --write --worktree --wait 0s --json --brief-file <brief-file>
{{end}}
Use `--read-only` for investigations and reviews. Use `--write` only when the user allows changes.
Never raise permissions yourself. Default model: deepseek-v4-flash (provider deepseek-official).
Preserve an explicit `--model`; efforts are off, low, high and max.
Resume with `--resume <job-id> --worktree` and the original cwd.

{{include "shared-delegation.md.tmpl"}}

Pactify uses `dsh --profile sdk`, pinned to the 0.2.1 SDK line. Read-only mode also
fails if the final repository diff is nonempty. Linked worktrees cannot git add/commit
because their git metadata is outside the sandbox; Pactify still collects the diff.
Default minimal config uses a private DSH_HOME with a credential link when present;
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY passes through. Never inspect credentials. `--with-user-config` keeps
sessions visible in the user's home. Telemetry is disabled in both modes.
Job TMPDIR is passed through; no extra writable roots or approval channel are available.
